# Note on the keep rule. All 3 miss peak_mae_feb by 0.003 to 0.010 ft against blend, which
# is under a tenth of an inch on 13 February cutoffs, while the gains at leads 12 to 24 are
# 3 to 10 times larger. The rule names only the peak, and this item targeted the far end.
# The headline stays `blend` until a person decides, because config/config.json names it.
# Caution: the split inside the covariate share swings between leads (accumulation h6 is
# 1.00 on swe_head, h9 is 0.65/0.35, h12 is 0.55/0.45). The share itself is well behaved.
# Open question 7, a smooth curve over the issue month, should come before any promotion.
# Lead 24 is unchanged in kind: blend_swe is still the best blend there at 1.855 ft, and
# naive_last still beats every model at 1.793 ft.
